I'm running 2.6.13-rc3 now but have been suffering from weird stalls with my
PPPoE connection ever since my ISP made it a requirement, about two months
ago. I found out by listening outgoing ethernet interface with tcpdump that
when a stall occurs, it's not sending anything. Listening to ppp interface
shows packets being sent. Discussed this with PPPoE maintainer Michal
Ostrowski and tried some debugging code he sent me, but it didn't reveal
really anything.

Here are two tcpdump logs taken when a stall occured and while a ping to ppp peer
